Does it work well with List?&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17022888" author="alex_pl" created="Fri, 24 Jan 2020 12:03:58 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=avinogradov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;avinogradov&quot;&gt;avinogradov&lt;/a&gt;, yes, it works well with List.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17022989" author="amashenkov" created="Fri, 24 Jan 2020 14:51:02 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;F.eq use equals method for comparing arrays.&lt;br/&gt;
I believe F.eq should compare arrays using Arrays.equals() instead.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="17023159" author="alex_pl" created="Fri, 24 Jan 2020 18:24:31 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?name=amashenkov&quot; class=&quot;user-hover&quot; rel=&quot;amashenkov&quot;&gt;amashenkov&lt;/a&gt;, I&apos;m not sure. &lt;tt&gt;F.eq&lt;/tt&gt;&#160;is widely used. I think it&apos;s safer to fix&#160;&lt;tt&gt;CacheEntryPredicateContainsValue&lt;/tt&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
